#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:60
msgid ""
"Add support for ``leeway`` parameter in JWT security backends, which allows "
"set a number of potential seconds as a clock error for expired tokens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:63
msgid ""
"``Token.decode`` and ``Token.decode_payload`` now take a ``leeway`` "
"argument. Custom token classes overriding either method must accept it and "
"forward to ``super()``, otherwise decoding raises ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:83
msgid ""
"Exceeding the configured multipart form part limit now returns ``413 Request "
"Entity Too Large`` instead of ``400 Bad Request``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:91
msgid ""
"The ``RapidocRenderPlugin`` has been removed due to lack of upstream "
"maintenance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:93
msgid ""
"Applications using ``RapidocRenderPlugin`` should migrate to another bundled "
"UI plugin, such as ``ScalarRenderPlugin`` (the default), "
"``SwaggerRenderPlugin``, ``RedocRenderPlugin`` or ``StoplightRenderPlugin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:103
msgid ""
"``ResponseCacheMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy "
"``AbstractMiddleware`` base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, "
"as part of migrating all built-in middleware off the legacy bases. It now "
"lives in ``litestar.middleware._internal``, removing it from the public API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:109
msgid ""
"The move into ``litestar.middleware._internal`` does not affect usage: the "
"middleware was only ever applied internally by Litestar to begin with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:112
msgid ""
"Applications that configure response caching through :class:`~litestar."
"config.response_cache.ResponseCacheConfig` and the handler-level ``cache`` "
"argument are unaffected -- Litestar constructs the middleware itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:116
msgid ""
"Code composing the middleware directly into an ASGI stack must drop the "
"``app`` argument, pass the settings as keyword arguments rather than a "
"``ResponseCacheConfig``, and apply the instance to the next ASGI app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:121
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"middleware = ResponseCacheMiddleware(app=next_app, "
"config=response_cache_config)\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"middleware = ResponseCacheMiddleware(\n"
"    default_expiration=response_cache_config.default_expiration,\n"
"    key_builder=response_cache_config.key_builder,\n"
"    store=response_cache_config.store,\n"
"    cache_response_filter=response_cache_config.cache_response_filter,\n"
")\n"
"asgi_app = middleware(next_app)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:134
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:171
msgid ""
"Since ``ASGIMiddleware.__call__`` returns a closure rather than the "
"middleware instance, a middleware stack can no longer be introspected by "
"walking the ``.app`` attribute of each layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:139
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:176
msgid ":ref:`asgi-middleware-migration`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:147
msgid ""
"``CORSMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy ``AbstractMiddleware`` "
"base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, as part of migrating "
"all built-in middleware off the legacy bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:151
msgid ""
"Applications that configure CORS through :class:`~litestar.config.cors."
"CORSConfig` are unaffected -- Litestar constructs the middleware itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:155
msgid ""
"Code instantiating the middleware directly must drop the ``app`` argument, "
"pass the settings as keyword arguments rather than a ``CORSConfig``, and "
"apply the instance to the next ASGI app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:160
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"middleware = CORSMiddleware(app=next_app, config=cors_config)\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"middleware = CORSMiddleware(allow_origins=cors_config.allow_origins, ...)\n"
"asgi_app = middleware(next_app)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:168
msgid ""
"The settings are copied on construction, so mutating ``CORSConfig`` after "
"the application has been created no longer affects the middleware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:202
msgid ""
"``httpx``, used by the test clients, has been moved from the default "
"dependencies to the ``litestar[testing]`` extra. It remains included in "
"``litestar[full]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:205
msgid ""
"Importing anything from ``litestar.testing`` without the extra installed now "
"raises a ``MissingDependencyException`` naming the extra to install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:209
msgid ":doc:`/usage/testing`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:216
msgid ""
"The ``litestar[cli]`` extra now requires ``rich-click>=1.9``. ``rich-click`` "
"was previously capped at ``<1.9``, which silently disabled the CLI's ``star-"
"box`` theme: the underlying ``theme`` option only exists from 1.9 onwards, "
"and assigning an unknown setting is ignored rather than raising."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:221
msgid ""
"The CLI configuration has been migrated off the options 1.9 deprecates "
"(``use_markdown`` / ``use_rich_markup`` in favour of ``text_markup``, and "
"``show_metavars_column`` / ``append_metavars_help`` in favour of "
"``options_table_column_types`` / ``options_table_help_sections``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:226
msgid ""
"The layout of the help output is preserved: option tables keep the long form "
"in the first column, the ``*`` marker on required parameters, and the "
"metavar appended directly after the help text. Colours do change, as the "
"``star-box`` theme now takes effect for the first time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:231
msgid ""
"This only affects applications that additionally pin ``rich-click<1.9`` "
"themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:235
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:251
msgid ":doc:`/usage/cli`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:242
msgid ""
"``click``, ``rich`` and ``rich-click``, which power the CLI, have been moved "
"from the default dependencies to the ``litestar[cli]`` extra. They remain "
"included in ``litestar[standard]`` and ``litestar[full]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:246
msgid ""
"Installing ``litestar`` on its own therefore no longer provides the "
"``litestar`` command. Invoking it without the extra now raises a "
"``MissingDependencyException`` naming the extra to install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:258
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib`` namespace. Integrations "
"previously available from this namespace have moved to their replacement "
"modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:266
msgid ""
"Remove declaring parameter and body metadata through default values and "
"setting defaults inside markers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:269
msgid ""
"The ``default`` keyword has been removed from ``Parameter`` and ``Body``, "
"along with the underlying ``KwargDefinition.default`` field. Passing it now "
"raises a ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:272
msgid ""
"Using a ``QueryParameter`` / ``HeaderParameter`` / ``PathParameter`` / "
"``CookieParameter`` or ``Body`` marker as a parameter *default value* (for "
"example ``data: Foo = Body(...)`` or ``param: int = QueryParameter(...)``) "
"now raises an exception"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:277
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:304
msgid "**Migration**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:279
msgid ""
"If metadata is declared on the marker, move the marker into ``Annotated``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:281
msgid ""
"``data: Foo = Body(min_items=2)`` becomes ``data: Annotated[Foo, "
"Body(min_items=2)]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:282
msgid ""
"``param: int = QueryParameter(gt=1)`` becomes ``param: Annotated[int, "
"QueryParameter(gt=1)]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:284
msgid ""
"For the unconstrained case the dedicated markers can be used as a shorthand, "
"e.g. ``JSONBody[Foo]``, ``MsgPackBody[Foo]``, ``MultipartBody[Foo]`` or "
"``URLEncodedBody[Foo]`` for bodies, and ``FromQuery[int]``, "
"``FromHeader[int]``, ``FromCookie[int]`` or ``FromPath[int]`` for parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:289
msgid ""
"Hoist defaults set inside ``Annotated`` into the parameter default: ``param: "
"Annotated[int, QueryParameter(default=5)]`` becomes ``param: Annotated[int, "
"QueryParameter(...)] = 5``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:301
msgid ""
"Remove ``params.Dependency`` and ``params.DependencyKwarg`` that were "
"deprecated in ``2.23.0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:306
msgid "Replace ``foo: int = Dependency()`` with ``foo: NamedDependency[int]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:307
msgid ""
"Replace ``foo: Annotated[int, Dependency(default=1)]`` by hoisting the "
"default into the parameter default: ``foo: NamedDependency[int] = 1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:309
msgid ""
"Replace ``foo: Annotated[int, Dependency(skip_validation=True)`` with ``foo: "
"NamedDependency[SkipValidation[int]]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:333
msgid "Drop support for Pydantic 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:335
msgid ""
"Pydantic 1 is no longer supported or tested against. No changes required for "
"applications already using Pydantic 2. Applications using Pydantic 1 or a "
"mix between 1 and 2 should upgrade to Pydantic 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:344
msgid ""
"Added optional ``ping_interval`` parameter to :class:`ServerSentEvent "
"<litestar.response.ServerSentEvent>` that sends SSE comment keepalive pings "
"at the specified interval to prevent connection timeouts from reverse "
"proxies or clients."
