#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:385
msgid ""
"Remove the default exception handler for all unhandled exceptions. Unhandled "
"exceptions will now be re-raised, for the server to handle. \"Unhandled "
"exceptions\" in this context means any exception for which no custom "
"exception handler exist, and that does not derive from :exc:"
"`LitestarException` or :exc:`HTTPException`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:393
msgid ""
"Your application's runtime behaviour won't change in terms of *if* "
"exceptions get handled. The main difference will be that, for an unhandled "
"exception, it will be the ASGI server that creates a ``500 - Internal Server "
"Error`` response, instead of Litestar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:420
msgid ""
"Remove all SQLAlchemy functionality from Litestar. Both ``litestar.contrib."
"sqlalchemy`` and ``litestar.plugins.sqlalchemy`` modules have been "
"completely removed. Users must now import directly from ``advanced_alchemy."
"extensions.litestar``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:424
msgid ""
"Migration: - ``from litestar.contrib.sqlalchemy import X`` → ``from "
"advanced_alchemy.extensions.litestar import X`` - ``from litestar.plugins."
"sqlalchemy import Y`` → ``from advanced_alchemy.extensions.litestar import "
"Y``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:428
msgid ""
"This completes the separation of concerns, with advanced-alchemy being the "
"sole provider of SQLAlchemy integration for Litestar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:437
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib.prometheus`` module. Code still "
"using imports from this module should switch to using ``litestar.plugins."
"prometheus``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:447
msgid ""
"Re-implement :class:`~litestar.testing.AsyncTestClient` to be async-native, "
"i.e. use the currently running event loop to run the application, instead of "
"running a separate event loop in a new thread. Additionally, a new :class:"
"`~litestar.testing.AsyncWebSocketTestSession` has been introduced, providing "
"an async testing utility for WebSockets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:452
msgid ""
"To ensure consisten behaviour across ``TestClient`` and ``AsyncTestClient``, "
"all testing utilities have been rewritten to be async first, with their "
"synchronous counterparts proxying calls to the async implementation, which "
"they run internally within a dedicated thread + event loop."
msgstr ""

